          "id": "binomial-introduction",
          "title": "Introduction",
          "lede": "When two binomials are multiplied, every term in one bracket must multiply every term in the other bracket.",
          "introduction": {
            "why": "Expanding brackets rewrites a product as one polynomial expression and prepares you for later algebraic manipulation.",
            "keyIdea": "Every term in the first bracket multiplies every term in the second bracket.",
            "method": [
              "Distribute each term across the other bracket.",
              "Keep the sign attached to each term.",
              "Collect like terms."
            ],
            "illustration": "(_x_ + 2)(_x_ + 5) → _x_^2 + 7_x_ + 10"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "binomial-video",
          "title": "Video",
